This class can be simplified by converting it to a `data class`. This is more idiomatic in Kotlin and will auto-generate `equals()`, `hashCode()`, `toString()`, and `copy()` methods, making the code more concise and maintainable. The separate `copy` extension function can also be removed.

```kotlin
public data class CacheSettings(
  public val storage: Storage = Storage.PERSISTENT,
) {

  /**
   * The types of cache storage supported by [FirebaseDataConnect] in its [CacheSettings] setting.
   */
  public enum class Storage {
    MEMORY,
    PERSISTENT,
  }
}
```

